      en: "Nsanje Boma, built in 1905, is a brick building with a colonial veranda. It served as the district headquarters and customs post near the Mozambican border. The town of Nsanje has 20,000 residents. The once-busy Shire River port closed in 1975. The boma now houses a regional museum. District population: 250,000.",
