      en: "Chizumulu Island Fortification was built in the 1890s by German colonists when the island was part of German East Africa. The stone fort, now ruined, sits 30 meters above the lake. Chizumulu has an area of 3 km² and a population of about 1000. The fort was used for defense against slave raiders. It became a British territory in 1919.",
